hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2844","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn, narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham, narrated to us Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn 'Abbas, from Usamah (RA), that the Prophet (ﷺ) made him ride behind him when he departed from 'Arafah. He (ﷺ) departed with tranquility and said: \"O people, adhere to tranquility, for indeed righteousness is not in urging on horses and camels.\"\n\nHe (RA) said: \"I did not see his camel raise its leg until he reached al-Jam'. Then he (ﷺ) made al-Fadl ride behind him, and he (ﷺ) ordered the people with tranquility and departed while tranquility was upon him, and he (ﷺ) said: 'Righteousness is not in urging on horses and camels.' I did not see his camel raise its leg until he reached Mina.\"\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
